---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import StatusNotice from '../components/StatusNotice.astro';

const pipeline = [
  ['Syntax models', 'Parse supported MathML into structured syntax data. LaTeX and AsciiMath follow later.'],
  ['Formula', 'Transform into the central Formula model, preserving supported presentation and style information. Unsupported input must receive an explicit refusal.'],
  ['Layout', 'Resolve style and font information into a private box tree without reparsing source or bypassing Formula.'],
  ['SVG', 'Emit deterministic SVG from the layout tree. Structural and visual checks are future qualification gates.'],
];
---
<Site title="Planned architecture" description="The intended Logifos rendering pipeline and delivery gates. No phase completion is claimed." page="architecture">
  <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="title">
    <p class="kicker">Architecture / design intent</p>
    <h1 id="title">From syntax<br />to a shared model.</h1>
    <p class="introduction">The intended architecture keeps formula meaning separate from layout and runtime delivery.</p>
    <StatusNotice />
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
    <h2 id="boundary-title">One planned JSON boundary</h2>
    <p>Every runtime is planned to enter through <code>logifos-facade</code>, with explicit operations and per-call options. All JSON decoding belongs to <code>logifos-json</code>. The target boundary returns typed failures and contains panics; the bootstrap does not implement that full contract.</p>
    <p>Rust owns parsing, transformation, layout and SVG. The planned Ruby and Python adapters use one portable native ABI; TypeScript uses WASM. Runtime wrappers do not contain another layout engine.</p>
    <p><a href="/api.html#contract">Read the pinned wire contract →</a></p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
    <h2 id="pipeline-title">Planned rendering path</h2>
    <ol class="pipeline">
      {pipeline.map(([name, detail]) => <li><h3>{name}</h3><p>{detail}</p></li>)}
    </ol>
    <p>A planned new syntax adds a <code>logifos-syntax-*</code> crate and its transformer. It does not change the layout or rendering core. The upstream Formula model and MathML syntax payload schemas still need authoritative pins; this site defines neither.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="fonts-title">
    <h2 id="fonts-title">Fonts and output</h2>
    <p>The planned Fontisan integration validates caller-supplied font bytes, faces and MATH data. Each call supplies hashes and an explicit fallback order; host fonts and network lookup are outside the target contract.</p>
    <p>SVG is the planned core output, with fixed ordering and no timestamps. Byte stability requires the same engine artifact, contract pins, options, font bytes and fallback order.</p>
    <p>PNG is planned only as Ruby-side conversion of qualified SVG through <code>svgpng</code>. The core contract refuses PNG. This scaffold provides neither SVG nor PNG rendering.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="gates-title">
    <h2 id="gates-title">Planned delivery gates</h2>
    <p>The planned gates cover MathML and Formula preservation, font-backed layout, SVG structure and visual results, installed runtime packages, then coordinated releases. A shared conformance corpus is planned to check the same behavior across transports.</p>
    <p>No phase completion is claimed by this site. Wrapper preparation can happen early; it does not satisfy a later rendering gate. Ruby and TypeScript launch together only after both qualify; Python follows.</p>
    <a href="/status.html">Return to current status →</a>
  </section>
</Site>
